post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
==> rs480-reset-hazard-stack installed.
    The RS480 failed-reset hazard safety substrate is present, but PRESENCE IS NOT SAFETY.
    Before every hazardous reset fire, run:

        rs480-reset-hazard-preflight   (or: rs480-reset-hazard-preflight --recovery)

    (The old name rad05-preflight still works but warns; use the new name.)

    It gates on the runtime facts a package cannot prove: watchdog substrate
    visibility, fired-latch fix installed, netconsole-rad05 active, lockup_timeout,
    and radeon srcversion match.

    Active watchdog feeding is RETIRED for RAD-05 fire timing: the SB600 reset is
    not deferrable via WDIOC_SETTIMEOUT, WDIOC_KEEPALIVE, or magic close. Hazard
    fires run WITHOUT the watchdog and use boot-persistent netconsole plus manual
    recovery. No watchdog is a sanctioned condition for RAD-05i/RAD-05j fires.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
